IVec timeout `507014`.\n\n**Recommendation**: Use `AscendC::CrossCoreSetFlag<MODE, PIPE>(flagId)` paired with `AscendC::CrossCoreWaitFlag(flagId)` as an explicit stage handoff. For `KERNEL_TYPE_MIX_AIC_1_2`, use `MODE = 0x2`, the AIC<->AIV paired sync mode. This is paired sub-block synchronization, not whole-device broadcast and not a `SyncAll<true>()` replacement.\n\nPipe selection:\n- Use `PIPE_FIX` when AIC produces data through FIX to GM.\n- Use `PIPE_MTE3` when AIV produces data through MTE3 to GM.\n- Choose the pipe whose retirement must precede the consumer read.\n\nFlag ownership:\n- User data flags are `0..FFTS_MAX_FLAG` = `0..7`.\n- IDs `8`, `9`, and `10` are reserved for barrier forms in the verified header; do not allocate them for user-owned data handoffs.\n- Existing canonical KB records same-flag max count / reverse-depth budget as 15. Do not design a ping-pong or counted protocol requiring more than 15 outstanding same-flag generations without separate source-level proof for that exact build.\n\nConcrete anchor:\n```cpp\nconstexpr uint32_t cubeOutReadyId = 1;\nconstexpr uint32_t vecOutReadyId  = 2;\n\n#ifdef __DAV_C220_CUBE__\n// AIC stage: after cube output through FIX is complete/ordered for handoff.\nAscendC::CrossCoreSetFlag<0x2, PIPE_FIX>(cubeOutReadyId);\n#endif\n\n#ifdef __DAV_C220_VEC__\n// AIV stage: wait before reading the cube intermediate.\nAscendC::CrossCoreWaitFlag(cubeOutReadyId);\n// ... vector compute writes its intermediate to GM through MTE3 ...\nAscendC::CrossCoreSetFlag<0x2, PIPE_MTE3>(vecOutReadyId);\n#endif\n\n#ifdef __DAV_C220_CUBE__\n// Later AIC stage: wait before reading the vector intermediate.\nAscendC::CrossCoreWaitFlag(vecOutReadyId);\n#endif\n```\n\n**Determinism**: This orders visibility only. It is data-flow deterministic only when every consumed GM region has exactly one producer for that handoff and the producer sets the flag after the producing pipe is ordered. Multi-producer aggregation needs a separate counted protocol and must respect the same-flag count budget.\n\n**Out of scope for this promoted rule**: `PIPE_MTE2` slot-free / \u201cconsumer finished reading\u201d queue release is plausible and appears in other mixed-mode examples, but it was not exercised by the FA evidence anchor. Promote that as a separate rule only after a shipped a5_ops or equivalent verified source anchor covers it.\n\n**Cross-references**:\n- P-P75: intra-core `SetFlag/WaitFlag<HardEvent>` pipe sync; this rule is cross-core AIC/AIV sync.\n- P-P68 / OL-91: `MatmulImpl` cube playbooks; these are excluded unless internal CrossCore flag use is proven isolated.",
